ry</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Cervicothoracic sympathectomy for Raynaud&#x02019;s syndrome</article-title><source>Int Angiol</source><year>1993</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8370999</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-wjem-9-0043"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sayers</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Jenner</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrie</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transthoracic endoscopic sympathectomy for hyperhidrosis and Raynaud&#x02019;s phenomenon</article-title><source>Eur J Vasc Surg</source><year>1994</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>627</fpage><lpage>631</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7813733</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-wjem-9-0043"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gifford</surname><given-names>RW</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Hines</surname><given-names>EA</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sympathectomy for Raynaud&#x02019;s phenomenon; follow-up study of 70 women with Raynaud&#x02019;s disease and 54 women and secondary Raynaud&#x02019;s phenomenon</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1958</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13511617</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17-wjem-9-0043"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Struthers</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>DGI</given-names></name><name><surname>Bacon</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Partial finger loss: an indicator of severe connective tissue disease with overlap features</article-title><source>Br J Rheumol</source><year>1983</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>217</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18-wjem-9-0043"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Landry</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Porter</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Current management of Raynaud&#x02019;s syndrome</article-title><source>Adv Surg</source><year>1996</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>347</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8960343</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-wjem-9-0043" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Necrotic fourth and fifth digits, five days after presentation of SLE patient with secondary Raynaud&#x02019;s phenomenon</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="wjem-9-0043f1"/></fig></floats-group></article>